  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000122924,
      "SummaryText": "The Branding Iron Holdings Rochester Frozen Facility, located at 4239 N. Frontage Rd., Rochester MN, is a production facility offering a wide range of meat products. Rochester Frozen uses Anhydrous Ammonia as a refrigerant at this facility to provide cooling for the production and storage areas. The Ammonia System falls under the EPA Risk Management Program due to the system quantity in excess of 10,000 lbs. The Rochester Meat refrigeration system is a closed loop system with normal operating pressures that range between a low side of O psi to a high side of 185 psi. The ammonia refrigeration system has a inventory is 21,300 pounds. \n\nProcess: The ammonia refrigeration system at the Rochester Frozen facility is a two stage system. Consisting of a high side and a low pressure side. The low side is intended to quickly freeze product, while the high side is intended to refrigerate the product. The Ammonia Refrigeration system is protected by built in safeties to prevent a run away system. The built in safeties include Safety Relief Valves, Engine Room Ventilation, and system interlocks for pressure, temperature and liquid levels. \n\nWorst-case Release Scenario for a Toxic Release and the Alternative Release Scenario for a Toxic Release can be found in the Hazard Assessment Report on file with Corporate. The Rochester Frozen facility. has established written Standard Operating Procedures and Safe Maintenance Procedures to operate and maintain the ammonia refrigeration system. The Rochester Frozen Facility. has also outlined and implemented a training program to assure that well trained refrigeration operators and trained HAZMAT responders can safely and properly operate the ammonia system. \n\nAlso. Rochester Frozen. is working with the Rochester Fire Dept. to coordinate efforts to minimize an offsite consequence that should occur. Rochester Frozen is very dedicated to aligning their of the ammonia system to meet all of the regulations under the OSHA and EPA rulings regard"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000122924,
      "SummaryText": "ing Anhydrous Ammonia."
    }
  ]
